WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.981
One set. Several repetitions.

00:00:03.372 --> 00:00:04.920
What should I look at next?

00:00:05.311 --> 00:00:10.511
Gym Bro organises the review: choose a
clip, inspect a moment, and read coaching

00:00:10.536 --> 00:00:12.873
cues alongside the measurements.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.840
Here is the app. The home page
offers an upload and a sample.

00:00:18.103 --> 00:00:22.873
We are opening the cached pull-up
example: real footage with a synthetic

00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:27.209
saved report. No live model
request is happening here.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.700
The results bring a selected
frame and its timestamp together.

00:00:31.824 --> 00:00:34.208
That gives the review a starting point.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:39.584
The timeline preserves context, so a
flagged moment need not stand alone.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.389
Toggle the skeleton overlay.

00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:46.760
The angle cards put the measured pose
beside the suggested target, while the

00:00:46.785 --> 00:00:48.763
coach explains the focus.

00:00:49.026 --> 00:00:53.285
These single-camera estimates do
not provide a complete assessment of

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.359
movement.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.305
The comparison makes the
visual idea easy to inspect.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:04.791
This demo&#x27;s after image is a later
real frame from the same clip: a

00:01:04.816 --> 00:01:09.098
placeholder for image editing,
which does not demonstrate an AI

00:01:09.123 --> 00:01:10.241
correction.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.798
When connected, sampled frames
follow a provider chain: Cosmos, then

00:01:15.823 --> 00:01:19.042
Nemotron, then GPT vision if needed.

00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:21.864
Pose measurement happens in the browser.

00:01:22.127 --> 00:01:26.676
Coaching and correction use those
measurements, followed by a primary-target

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:27.645
check.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.572
Open the trace panel. These
entries are cached example data.

00:01:32.777 --> 00:01:38.087
In a connected run, the panel helps
inspect attempts, timings and fallbacks.

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.551
A trace explains execution;
it does not establish coaching

00:01:42.576 --> 00:01:43.752
accuracy.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.877
The library is separate from analysis.

00:01:47.082 --> 00:01:52.043
It searches existing VAST-indexed
workout clips using a team key.

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:55.909
Uploading a video for analysis
does not save it here.

00:01:56.231 --> 00:02:01.378
Today, the real interface correctly
shows that the library is not configured.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.518
Optional Weave traces record provider,
model, duration, outcome and an

00:02:07.543 --> 00:02:12.696
error category. The exporter excludes
images, prompts, coaching text

00:02:12.721 --> 00:02:16.522
and search queries. It
is disabled by default.

00:02:16.912 --> 00:02:19.889
Export failure cannot fail the analysis.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:25.891
Local tests and synthetic checks cover
software contracts, access controls

00:02:25.916 --> 00:02:28.741
and tracing policy, not form accuracy.

00:02:29.131 --> 00:02:34.285
Next, retrieve a known gym clip, read
back a real Weave trace, and evaluate

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.484
judgements against labelled movements.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.527
CoreWeave GPU hosting remains a proposal.

00:02:40.686 --> 00:02:45.548
Test the existing Cosmos payload against
a suitable endpoint, then compare

00:02:45.573 --> 00:02:50.848
quality, latency, fallbacks and
cost before changing the default.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.682
That is Gym Bro: inspect the moment,
understand the cue, and keep the

00:02:56.707 --> 00:02:59.729
evidence visible as the project grows.
